<title>DUBAI: ADNOC invites bids for Asab field expansion.</title>
<headline>ADNOC invites bids for Asab field expansion.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Abu Dhabi National Oil Co (ADNOC) has invited seven international firms to submit bids for the $680 million expansion of the onshore Asab gas field, the UAE daily Emirates News reported on Monday.</p>
<p>Bidders include U.S Bechtel, Italy's Snamprogetti, France's Technip and Japan's Mitsubishi Heavy Industries, Chiyoda Corp, Tokyo Engineering and JGC, the paper quoted a market source as saying.</p>
<p>The Asab project is a major element of ADNOC's plan to develop its gas reserves to keep pace with rising local demand and to meet gas reinjection and condensate output targets.</p>
<p>&quot;The companies have been asked to return their bids by the middle of December. They will be given 30 months to complete the work,&quot; the source told Emirates News.</p>
<p>-- Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255</p>
</text>
